<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaiya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chaiya is a town and district in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surat-thani">Surat Thani</a> province in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bandon">Bay of Bandon</a>. An important centre in the era of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>, it is known for the temple of Wat Phra Borommathat Chaiya and for Buddhist sculptures and inscriptions, among them an inscription of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrabhanu">Chandrabhanu</a> of Tambralinga dated 1230.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chaiya.jpg" alt="Chaiya" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KOSIN SUKHUM · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wat_Phra_Boromathat_Chaiya_(Thailand).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
